                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "236660370",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199057223584",
                            "num_reviews": 6,
                            "playtime_forever": 1575,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1524,
                            "last_played": 1790979677
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a simple puzzle game with soothing music. I'm not very good at majong because I suck at planning out more than three or four moves ahead but I'm still having fun. The art style is pretty. You also don't need to get complete mastery over every level to advance further through the game. Each level has three things to get full mastery, pass within a certain number of moves, get above a certain score and of course get all the gold tiles. There's several mythical creatures in cages. Each cage has a cluster of levels. Getting two of the three on most of the levels per creature seems to be enough to unlock the next set of levels. If your working memory is kind of bad like mine it can be a little frustrating. It's easy enough though that if I'm getting frustrated it's probably over tiredness and low blood sugar. It's great for killing an hour here and there every once in awhile when I want a puzzle game but I'm too tired or over stimulated for a match three game.",
